  "question": {
    "text": "The sum of all values of $\\theta \\in[0,2 \\pi]$ satisfying $2 \\sin ^2 \\theta=\\cos 2 \\theta$ and $2 \\cos ^2 \\theta=3 \\sin \\theta$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "9CAq7",
      "text": "$4 \\pi$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "P2jYw",
      "text": "$\\frac{5 \\pi}{6}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qpHyt",
      "text": "$\\pi$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "IkkNO",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& 2 \\sin ^2 \\theta=\\cos 2 \\theta \\\\\n& 2 \\sin ^2 \\theta=1-2 \\sin ^2 \\theta \\\\\n& 4 \\sin ^2 \\theta=1 \\\\\n& \\sin ^2 \\theta=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\\n& \\sin \\theta= \\pm \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n& 2 \\cos ^2 \\theta=3 \\sin \\theta \\\\\n& 2-2 \\sin ^2 \\theta+3 \\sin \\theta-2=0 \\\\\n& (2 \\sin \\theta-1)(2 \\sin \\theta-2)=0 \\\\\n& \\sin \\theta=\\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}$\nso common equation which satisfy both equations is $\\sin \\theta=\\frac{1}{2}$\n$\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{6}, \\frac{5 \\pi}{6} \\quad(\\theta \\in[0,2 \\pi])$\n\nSum $=\\pi$",
    "image": null
  },
